  story:[ "<p>Clinics across three states are recalling injections while laboratories compare patient isolates with the compounding facility.</p>", "<p><b>Pharmacy Tech Ruiz</b> filled the vials, <b>The Micro Analyst</b> read the environmental cultures, and <b>The Clerk</b> holds the release records.</p>", "<p><b>A deliberate poisoning of the medicine</b> and <b>A run of coincidental illnesses — bad luck</b> ignore the production controls that should connect distant illnesses to one source.</p>", "<p>The remaining lots reach their use dates in eight days, forcing a decision before every culture has finished growing.</p>" ],
  endings:{ overclaimWhat:"poison", dismissalWhat:"coincidence",
    win:{ expertTitle:"The Contamination Has a Batch", expert:["You identify <b>Guillory — the pharmacy's owner</b>, trace batch release to <b>The Owner's Business Office</b>, and establish <b>Sterility controls cut and contamination ignored to raise output</b>. Not a deliberate poisoning of the medicine; not a run of coincidental illnesses — bad luck.","Shortened sterilization, unchecked hoods, positive environmental plates, and release overrides connect one production decision with illnesses across several states."], soundTitle:"Sterility Reconstructed", sound:["The batch history supports your conclusion against <b>Guillory — the pharmacy's owner</b> for <b>Sterility controls cut and contamination ignored to raise output</b>, documented in <b>The Owner's Business Office</b>.","Not every contaminated vial can be recovered, but process deviations and matching clinical isolates already establish an unsafe release system."], namedTitle:"The Released Failure", named:["Your pharmacy accusation correctly names <b>Guillory — the pharmacy's owner</b>, <b>The Owner's Business Office</b>, and <b>Sterility controls cut and contamination ignored to raise output</b>.","It needs fuller microbiology, yet it sends investigators to the autoclave records, monitoring plates, and batch-release stamps."] },
    overclaim:{ title:"No Hand Added Poison", body:["You choose <b>A deliberate poisoning of the medicine</b>, searching for an added toxin while the facility’s microbial controls document their own collapse.","The poison theory fails and gives defenders an opening to portray the genuine contamination evidence as another exaggeration."] },
    dismissal:{ title:"Coincidence Did Not Share a Lot", body:["You accept <b>A run of coincidental illnesses — bad luck</b>, treating geographically linked infections as unrelated misfortune.","Shared lots, organisms, and production dates contradict coincidence and leave remaining inventory dangerously unresolved."] },
    wrongNames:{ title:"Right Contamination, Wrong Signatory", body:["You recognize <b>Sterility controls cut and contamination ignored to raise output</b>, but blame the wrong pharmacy employee or move the release authority outside the business office. The signed deviations lead to"] } },
